[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_b1nds")
titel = "Wild-Folk"
description = "Wild-folk is the term Imperial scholars use to group the semi-civilized, predominantly male races of the world.

Wild-folk populations are overwhelmingly male, with only one in every ten to twenty births producing a female child. This imbalance forces them to interbreed with tall-folk to sustain their populations. In the past, this led to constant conflict between wild-folk and the tall-folk (mostly represented by the Lyrian Empire). It also created a deeply ingrained tradition of kidnapping and enslaving tall-folk women, both as human cattle and as breeding slaves.

Over the last few centuries, the Lyrian Empire has allied itself with many wild-folk tribes along its borders, forming an uneasy alliance based on trade and mutual defence. These agreements also tolerate traditional wild-folk slavery, provided it remains mostly consensual.

Goblins and orks are the most common wild-folk, although orks are far less likely to ally with tall-folk. Kobolds are also considered wild-folk, but are relatively rare in the Borderlands.

The classification of halflings remains somewhat disputed because of their highly civilized society. However, they are predominantly male and practise human cattle slavery, so most scholars categorize them as wild-folk."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://bkxhc74auednr"
